Dear Robert,

During the ATU-100 UT thickness survey, field work recorded in LNDE-FN-20241025-031 identified that CML 4-RA-101-06 has reached a thickness of 3.59 mm. This reading is below the retirement thickness of 3.81 mm. Consequently, QSCP-NCR-2024-031 has been issued to document this nonconformance.

The short-term corrosion rate has increased to 0.664 mm/y, resulting in an expired remaining life for this location. Please review the findings for the rich amine line 4-RA-101 to determine the required mitigation or repair scope.

Regards,  Jennifer Walsh Inspection Coordinator QSCP Hamilton Inspection Department  CC: Robert Hendricks

